<title>ITALY: Specialist bondtraders make no bids for Italy CTZ.</title>
<headline>Specialist bondtraders make no bids for Italy CTZ.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders made no bids for two-year zero couponed certificates (CTZs) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 250 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 3.73 trillion lire at the open auction for the January 15, 1999 paper, against 2.5 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 89.25 from 88.85 at the previous CTZ sale on January 10.</p>
</text>
